      'Treatment of amblyopia: refractive correction first, then occlusion or atropine penalisation.',
      'Esotropia: infantile (large angle, onset <6 months), accommodative (refractive), partially accommodative.',
      'Exotropia: intermittent (most common), constant, sensory.',
      'Inferior oblique overaction: V-pattern strabismus; treat with IO weakening procedures.',
      'Brown syndrome: limited elevation in adduction; congenital (tight superior oblique tendon) or acquired (trauma, inflammation).',
      'Duane retraction syndrome: type I (limited abduction), type II (limited adduction), type III (both); CN VI nucleus abnormality with aberrant CN III innervation.',
      'Leukocoria differential: retinoblastoma, congenital cataract, Coats disease, PHPV, ROP, toxocariasis.',
      'Retinoblastoma: most common intraocular malignancy of childhood; RB1 gene on 13q14.',
